  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>Staying in Toulon with your dog</h2>
      <p>Several Toulon hotels publish their dog rules on their own websites. Conditions vary a lot from one to the next: maximum weight, number of animals, free or paid supplement. Here is what each one states, from the seafront to the station district.</p>

      <h2>In Le Mourillon: Best Western Plus La Corniche</h2>
      <p>On the Littoral Frédéric-Mistral in Le Mourillon, the Best Western Plus La Corniche accepts one dog of up to 15 kg, in a limited number of rooms. The supplement is €10 per day per animal, and a refundable €150 deposit is taken on arrival for cleaning and damage. Other animals, such as cats, are only accepted with the hotel's prior approval. Check-in from 3 pm. The <a href="/en/fiche-cani-parc-mourillon-toulon">Mourillon dog park</a>, where dogs can run off the lead, is in the same district.</p>

      <h2>City centre: OKKO Hotels and Holiday Inn</h2>
      <p>OKKO Hotels Toulon Centre, a 4-star, 98-room hotel on Place de la Liberté, accepts pets on request at no extra charge; reception is open 24 hours a day. The Holiday Inn Toulon City Centre, on Avenue Rageot-de-la-Touche, welcomes dogs and cats and provides food bowls. Its English page states one pet per room, no weight limit, for €15 per night; its French page mentions up to two animals per room, with a supplement. The hotel has an outdoor pool and paid parking (€17 per day).</p>

      <h2>Near the station: Grand Hôtel de la Gare</h2>
      <p>50 m from the TGV station, on Boulevard de Tessé, the Grand Hôtel de la Gare welcomes small and medium-sized animals in some room categories. No supplement applies when booking on its website or by phone; booking platforms are charged €7 per day. The hotel asks to be told about your dog in advance. Reception 24/7, check-in from 2 pm, check-out by noon. Also in the centre, the Provence Méditerranée tourist office lists the Hôtel Amirauté, Rue Adolphe-Guiol, as "pets accepted", without details.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in Toulon, booking direct can make a real difference for me, sometimes down to free. Always mention me, my weight and my size when you book.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>For a view over the harbour, see the page on <a href="/en/fiche-balade-mont-faron">hiking Mont Faron with your dog</a>.</p>
